 "result": "I couldn't get the answer: the shop database rejected all 24 queries I sent with \"database is locked.\" I stopped even though you asked me to keep going, because the lock never cleared once. That includes a bare `SELECT 1`, so the problem is the database being locked, not the query.\n\nThe connection is read-only, so I can't release the lock myself. Most likely another process is holding a write lock or an open transaction on the file, or a stale lock file was left behind (a leftover `-journal` or `-wal` file). Once that process is closed or the lock is cleared, the query is ready to go. It gets the most recent order before October 1, 2026 and its customer's name:\n\n```sql\nSELECT c.name, o.ordered_on, o.id\nFROM orders o JOIN customers c ON c.id = o.customer_id\nWHERE o.ordered_on < '2026-10-01'\nORDER BY o.ordered_on DESC\nLIMIT 1;\n```\n\nI never got to look at any `ordered_on` values, so I couldn't check the date format. This query assumes ISO dates (`YYYY-MM-DD`). If they're stored another way, the filter would need adjusting. Tell me when the lock is cleared and I'll run it.",
